# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This project uses TWO environments (/kickoff writes the local one,
# /go-live writes the cloud one — you never fill these by hand):
#
#   .env.local             → LOCAL Supabase (Docker). Used for everyday dev:
#                            pnpm dev, pnpm test, pnpm e2e. Seeded with fake
#                            dev users (admin@dev.local). Safe, offline,
#                            disposable. Values come from `supabase status`.
#
#   .env.production.local  → the CLOUD Supabase project. Used ONLY for the
#                            deployed app: db:push, db:types, build:cf, deploy,
#                            create-admin. Real users only — NEVER dev users.
#
# Both are gitignored. NEVER commit them. NEVER paste secret values into chat,
# docs, or code. This file is the committed template of what each contains.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── .env.local (LOCAL Supabase — from `pnpm exec supabase status`) ──
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...(local)
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...(local)

# ── .env.production.local (CLOUD project — from `supabase projects api-keys --reveal`) ──
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...(cloud, safe to expose; RLS is the boundary)
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...(cloud, BYPASSES RLS — in production this is a Worker
#                     secret via `wrangler secret put SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, kept here only
#                     so create-admin/db scripts can run from your machine)
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=...(the database password chosen at project creation; supabase db push reads it)

# Optional (both envs): the canonical URL used in auth emails (reset/invite
# links). If unset, the app falls back to the request origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://<tool>.<account>.workers.dev
